      "body": "## Motivation\n`TokenizerControlMixin.start_profile` fills an unset `ProfileReq.with_stack` / `record_shapes` from `SGLANG_PROFILE_WITH_STACK` / `SGLANG_PROFILE_RECORD_SHAPES` (both default `true`) before the request leaves the tokenizer process. By the time a platform's scheduler-side profiler sees the request, \"unset\" and \"explicitly true\" are indistinguishable.\nAn out-of-tree platform may want server-wide capture defaults (for example, stacks and shapes off by default because they add noise to device traces, or a default `num_steps`) while still letting explicit `/start_profile` fields override them. Today that requires monkey-patching `start_profile`.\n## Modifications\n- Add `SRTPlatform.apply_profile_request_defaults(req: ProfileReq) -> None` to `sglang/srt/platforms/interface.py`. The base implementation is a no-op, so in-tree platforms behave exactly as before.\n- Call it at the start of `TokenizerControlMixin.start_profile`, right after the request type is set and before the env-based normalization. The env vars still apply afterwards, so `SGLANG_PROFILE_WITH_STACK=false` / `SGLANG_PROFILE_RECORD_SHAPES=false` continue to force those options off.\n- Add `test/registered/unit/managers/test_tokenizer_control_mixin.py`, which checks that a platform's defaults for unset fields reach the scheduler-bound request even though both env vars are `true`, both for `start_profile()` with no request and with an empty `ProfileReq()`.\n## Testing\n```bash\npython3 test/registered/unit/managers/test_tokenizer_control_mixin.py      # 1 test, OK\npython3 test/registered/unit/platforms/test_platform_interface.py          # 74 tests, OK\npython3 test/registered/unit/managers/test_lora_update_result_merge.py     # 3 tests, OK\npython3 test/registered/unit/managers/test_tokenizer_config_updates.py     # 10 tests, OK\n```\nThe new test fails on `main` without the `start_profile` call (the platform sees `with_stack=True` / `record_shapes=True` already filled from the env defaults).\n## Accuracy Tests\nN/A, profiling control path only.\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\nN/A.\n## Checklist\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41761812163](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41761812163)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41761812011](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41761812011)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #41761812050](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41761812050)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
